WEBVTT

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:13.810
Hunting a monster.

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:19.050
Akagi agreed to Ougi and 
Yasuoka's outrageous proposal.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:25.160
His heart was moved by this mechanism 
of a challenge that brings death.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:29.670
And he picked up a scent in the 
monster that was similar to his own.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:32.160
<i>He is bored.</i>

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:34.170
<i>Just like me.</i>

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:41.430
<i>He's tired of living.</i>

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:47.620
<i>This man stands alone 
and hopelessly bored</i>

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:51.090
<i>at the summit of the 
mountain they call success.</i>

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:54.510
<i>His whole life was filled with success,</i>

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.730
<i>but now it's past its expiration date.</i>

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:00.470
<i>It can't intoxicate him anymore.</i>

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:03.560
<i>You're like a giant serpent 
being roasted alive.</i>

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.000
<i>I can't die yet.</i>

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.120
<i>There must be something else...</i>

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:11.820
<i>Except there isn't.</i>

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.250
<i>So just die already, you heretic.</i>

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.190
<i>That is your only salvation.</i>

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.490
<i>You and I will never be understood.</i>

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:20.910
<i>We're just outcasts.</i>

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:24.640
<i>We are of the same kind.</i>

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.690
<b>Episode 15</b>

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.690
<b>The Witching Hour</b>

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:34.430
<b>The 
Inada 
Group</b>

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:30.890
After Akagi got back to Tokyo,

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:34.430
he stayed with the Inada Group, 
where Ougi was the second in command.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:38.930
Akagi now waits for his moment 
to approach the monster,

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:41.940
for the negotiations to close.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:45.440
Akagi imagines the monster.

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:48.270
What is that man's core?

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:52.470
Washizu Iwao.

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:57.680
Washizu graduated from the 
Old Imperial University in 1912.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.740
He joined the investigative 
bureau at the age of 22,

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:01.890
what is called the police force today.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.450
He distinguished himself considerably

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.890
with his brilliant intelligence and ambition.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.800
In 1932, at the age of 42,

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.900
he became the superintendent 
of a special police unit.

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:14.400
And in 1940, at the age of 50,

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:19.640
he rose to the position of what would 
be the Chief Commissioner today.

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:24.140
But in 1942 he suddenly retired.

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:28.460
Washizu foresaw...

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:31.340
the destruction of this country.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:36.150
Undoubtedly, he has the ability to 
see one or two steps into the future;

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.030
a remarkable sense of foresight.

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:43.860
<b>Kyousei 
Consulting</b>

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:43.860
After the war, 
Washizu started a consulting firm.

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:46.100
He possessed knowledge of

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:49.370
many a politician's scandals 
from his time in the police,

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:53.100
and he used it to obtain 
information from them.

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:55.950
This meant he knew what 
places would be developed,

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.000
what laws would be lifted.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:06.380
With this valuable information, 
he was able to consult with many firms.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:09.820
Of course, Washizu's advice 
was always spot on.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:11.630
Those firms grew rapidly,

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:15.440
and he continued to skim a 
percentage of the profits.

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:19.320
He amassed a seemingly 
infinite amount of money.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.470
Money that continued to increase.

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:22.430
Money.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:26.820
Next thing he knew, he was 
standing all alone at the summit.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.280
In his grip, he held the power of money

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:32.080
as well as the secrets of 
politicians and business men.

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:36.130
Nobody was any longer in a position 
to point a finger at him.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:38.450
He was an absolute power 
overwhelming all others.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.840
The hidden king who rules the 
country from the shadows.

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:47.260
But then, this undefeated man fell 
victim to old age... and insanity.

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:53.290
The shrewd man who had overcome the 
changing times by his own power

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:55.960
and had such control over himself 
ended up destroying his own spirit.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:00.340
Most likely through despair 
so overwhelmingly deep,

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:04.340
the average person cannot 
even hope to comprehend it.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.170
<i>Why can't I be satisfied?</i>

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:09.340
<i>Why must I die?</i>

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:10.930
<i>Of course you'll die.</i>

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:13.020
<i>Even the greatest kings die.</i>

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:17.080
<i>Your mistake was closing 
your eyes to that truth.</i>

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.780
<i>I bet he hates people 
just for being young.</i>

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:24.830
<i>What is this? What is this?</i>

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.720
<i>A piece of trash with no
intelligence or talent,</i>

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.700
<i>but he will outlive me.</i>

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:31.190
<i>I won't allow it.</i>

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:32.940
<i>I won't allow it.</i>

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:35.340
<i>I won't allow it!</i>

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:42.620
It's August, 1965.

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:48.350
For the first time in his 75 years, 
the monster Washizu Iwao was in trouble.

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:52.530
His arrest was imminent.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:57.750
Witnesses testified to the meeting 
of Fake Akagi and Washizu's underlings.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:01.460
Items found at the site of the 
buried corpse matched items

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:03.210
that had been used in Washizu's home.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.540
The tire tracks at the scene matched those

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:07.300
of a car found at his mansion.

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:10.920
There was nowhere left to run,

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:13.840
but Washizu still escaped 
the predicament cleverly.

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:17.050
Using his vast fortune,

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:20.510
he bribed high-ranking politicians 
and members of the police.

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:23.990
He also blackmailed them by threatening

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:26.320
to expose their scandals to the public.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:31.390
Mixing these soft and hard methods, 
he slowly turned the situation around.

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:33.830
He got away.

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:41.000
It looks like the last local cop who was 
still against me gave in to the bribe.

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:43.770
You can all rest assured.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:45.870
I made it fit.

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:48.110
Congratulations, sir.

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:50.840
Of course.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:52.760
This is the natural outcome.

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:55.450
Of course they would want 
to cover up a murder

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:57.720
committed by a former police officer.

00:06:57.720 --> 00:06:59.650
This is the natural outcome.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:04.460
Though, those stubborn fools did 
extort quite a sum out of me.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:07.470
But it's all the same.

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:09.960
No matter how much I give them, 
I can always get it back.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:14.720
I know all of their secrets.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:17.040
It's not a problem.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.840
I won't fall.

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:21.440
I will never fall.

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:26.540
However, they say I have to 
leave the country for a while.

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:30.340
I wouldn't normally excuse such 
insolence committed against me

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.550
by the country I have 
devoted my life to serving,

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:36.120
but it looks like the media is 
close to uncovering something.

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:37.550
Yoshioka.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:38.380
I have no choice.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:40.130
Will you accompany me?

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:42.060
Yes, of course, I will.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:45.750
Your entire fortune, 
including the worth of this mansion,

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:49.430
is ready to be liquefied at any 
time and accompany you, as well.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:52.890
You could hide yourself for years.

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:55.630
Yoshioka.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:59.940
How dare you suggest I "hide" myself?

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:04.410
Have you forgotten all I 
have done for this country?

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:08.050
I laid the very foundations 
for this nation!

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.550
Have you forgotten my contributions?

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:18.980
Compared to such 
overwhelming contributions,

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:21.330
how can anything I do be a problem?!

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:26.330
It's no problem if I decide to 
kill five or six useless punks.

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:28.970
They should allow me to do that.

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:30.880
Am I wrong, Yoshioka?

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:33.190
It is as you say, sir.

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:40.810
I want you to contact Ougi.

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:43.690
It seems they have someone 
who could play me.

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:46.800
Sir, but it is precisely 
that game that has—

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:47.710
Silence.

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:51.420
I only have a few more 
days left in Japan.

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:56.300
Tonight is my last supper.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.570
Stop your bellyaching.

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:00.930
The showdown will be tonight.

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.570
Call him right now.

00:09:02.570 --> 00:09:03.740
Hurry up.

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:04.640
Yes, sir!

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:11.580
Akagi had stayed with the 
Inada Group for two weeks.

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:21.570
Akagi, we're going.

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:26.720
The time to play against 
Washizu Iwao had finally arrived.

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:32.330
At 9 PM, three cars depart 
for the Washizu mansion.

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:36.940
Two of the cars hold armed 
members of the Inada gang,

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:39.810
who are going along to make sure 
the terms of the game are upheld.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:44.490
Ougi, Yasuoka and Akagi 
ride in the first car.

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:45.870
Ougi-san.

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:46.810
Yeah?

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.280
There's a place I'd like to 
stop at on the way.

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:51.290
Where?

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:57.230
A doctor?

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:59.320
Is his shoulder not healed yet?

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:02.130
It seems it has not 
completely healed yet, no.

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:05.160
Thanks for waiting.

00:10:06.590 --> 00:10:09.460
Is the wound on your shoulder okay?

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:12.240
It's totally fine.

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:15.540
I went for these.

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:17.040
Energy drinks?

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:20.290
I just wanted something, 
anything, to hydrate me.

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:25.920
I'm not about to drink a single 
drop of anything they offer us there.

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:28.300
Sorry!

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:31.420
We're the ones who should 
have thought of that.

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:35.190
They wouldn't think 
twice about drugging us,

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:38.300
seeing as we're trying to 
take 500 million from them.

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:44.300
500 million yen in 1965 would 
be over five billion yen today.

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:48.280
There's no such thing 
as being too cautious.

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:51.690
At 10 PM,

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:54.780
Akagi steps inside at last.

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:30.410
So you're my opponent for the night.

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:32.040
Yeah.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:33.150
My, are you young!

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:34.330
But that's good.

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:35.020
That's good.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:37.240
Youth is valuable.

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:41.020
It's perfectly proportional to the 
huge sum I'm putting on the line.

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:44.390
Then, why don't we start...

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.430
this game of Washizu Mahjong right away?

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:09.680
I still haven't caught your name.

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:10.880
Akagi.

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:13.420
Akagi-kun, is it?

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:14.830
Take a seat.

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:19.630
I'm sure they've briefed you already,

00:12:20.310 --> 00:12:23.130
but before we start playing, 
I need to explain a few things...

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:28.000
about the house rules of 
this mansion's Mahjong.

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:32.510
In general, though, the rules 
are the same as anywhere else.

00:12:32.990 --> 00:12:35.130
What's different is the tools we use.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:38.670
I'm fairly certain this is 
the first time you've seen these.

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:42.380
So those are Washizu Mahjong tiles...

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:49.250
We will be using these transparent tiles, 
which can be read even when facedown.

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:52.780
Three out of the four of each 
kind of tile is transparent.

00:12:52.780 --> 00:12:56.500
Only one of the four is a 
regular tile with a back black.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.110
As you'll find out,

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:00.500
you'll find yourself getting stuck often.

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:03.240
You won't be able to discard 
because you can see almost everything.

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.140
Imagine if you were 
walking along a path

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:08.740
and suddenly you were informed 
it was actually a minefield.

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:11.100
You wouldn't be able to take a 
single step further, am I right?

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:13.110
This is just like that.

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:16.710
These transparent tiles are a tool 
to make those land mines visible.

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:20.220
It's an intriguing execution, am I right?

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:23.480
Awareness breeds fear.

00:13:23.970 --> 00:13:26.910
People tremble only after 
they have become aware.

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:29.650
And it is watching 
people become aware

00:13:29.650 --> 00:13:33.400
and start to tremble 
that I find so amusing.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.140
Now, as for the house rules.

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:42.430
More than rules, 
they are adjustments to make

00:13:42.430 --> 00:13:44.640
playing Mahjong with 
transparent tiles possible.

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:48.250
There are three rules altogether.

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:51.780
The first is that no wall will be built.

00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:54.320
It's no fun if you know the 
next tile you will draw.

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:58.140
In Washizu Mahjong, 
the tiles for the starting hand

00:13:58.140 --> 00:14:01.460
and each draw are taken from the 
hole in the middle of the table.

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:02.940
The second rule is that

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:04.210
draws are made with a leather glove,

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:06.460
so that the tiles can't 
be read with the fingers.

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:08.740
The third rule regards 
the indicators for dora,

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:11.470
reverse dora, and new dora from kan.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:15.200
After everybody has their starting hand, 
the dealer draws one more tile from the hole

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:18.160
to be the dora indicator for that hand.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:20.270
The same method will be 
applied for reverse dora

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:23.980
and kan dora as the need arises.

00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:28.450
To avoid cheating, a machine 
will shuffle all the tiles.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:31.470
The machine will automatically 
shuffle the tiles

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:33.550
when someone touches the 
metal rim of the hole.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:35.470
What do you think?

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:36.460
Pretty interesting, huh?

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:39.600
But the problem is still ahead.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:44.200
Not even Ougi-kun knows about the 
rule I am about to reveal to you.

00:14:45.430 --> 00:14:50.140
There was a time when I used to 
play Mahjong for hundreds of millions.

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:55.030
For a while I was quite enthralled, 
but now it's no more than a distraction.

00:14:55.030 --> 00:14:57.310
It's not enough for me anymore.

00:14:57.940 --> 00:15:00.160
My tastes have gone elsewhere.

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:03.080
To make a long story short, 
I'm wagering something else.

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:04.070
That is to say...

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:05.320
I have a good idea what it is.

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:09.290
You mean... the player's blood.

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:13.530
You're telling me to bet my blood, right?

00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:19.180
You got it!

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:21.000
You're a sharp one.

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:24.520
If you figured that out based on 
these serial incidents of late,

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:25.870
this will be a quick explanation.

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:27.760
You are exactly right.

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:30.240
I am asking you to 
bet your own blood.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:33.110
If you lose, you die.

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:40.680
The human body has approximately 
four to five liters of blood.

00:15:40.680 --> 00:15:44.590
Judging by your size, I'd say 
you have about 4.5 liters.

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:48.300
You wouldn't be betting 
all of that amount.

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:49.660
Of course not.

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:53.970
You would die long before all 
your blood has been drawn.

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:58.300
It also depends on the speed with 
which one loses blood, but death

00:15:58.300 --> 00:16:01.780
generally starts creeping 
in once the body loses about

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:03.760
a third of its blood supply.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:08.270
Usually the blood loss is 
fatal before the 50% mark.

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:12.620
You have about 2,000 
CCs of blood to bet.

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:15.160
That is the lethal amount for you.

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:16.880
Were it to be drawn quickly,

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:20.630
even 1,500 CCs would be 
enough to kill you.

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:23.960
But even if you didn't die, 
your mind would be so muddled

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:27.600
that you would be in no 
condition to play Mahjong.

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:32.640
Considering all that, we can say 
that your limit is 1,500 CCs.

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:37.010
But I will be aiming at the amount 
that will, undoubtedly, kill you.

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:39.620
There is no point in 
merely weakening you.

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:43.480
You will continue playing 
to your last breath,

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:47.070
even if it means croaking 
right here on this table.

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:49.990
You will not be allowed to withdraw 
in the middle of the game.

00:16:49.990 --> 00:16:52.960
2,000 CCs are the price of your life.

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:56.930
And that price is 20 million.

00:16:57.960 --> 00:17:01.930
20 million yen in 1965 would 
be over 200 million yen today.

00:17:02.590 --> 00:17:05.930
You can have enough fun for the 
rest of your life with that money.

00:17:05.930 --> 00:17:09.640
With some restraint, you will 
never have to work again.

00:17:09.640 --> 00:17:12.680
What do you say? Worth betting 
your life, don't you think?

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:20.280
Now, how do we convert my money 
and your blood into Mahjong points?

00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:25.290
I'd say that 200,000 points 
would be the appropriate amount.

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:29.540
If you lose 200,000 points 
during six East-South matches,

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:32.640
you will lose 2,000 CCs of blood and die.

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:38.070
However, should you complete all six 
with enough blood left to survive,

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:41.900
you will have more money than you could 
ever earn through a lifetime of work.

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:46.410
But as for those 200,000 points 
in six East-South matches...

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:50.290
This is a one-on-one battle 
between you and me.

00:17:50.780 --> 00:17:54.000
We are competing only against 
each other for points.

00:17:55.610 --> 00:18:00.020
Let's say I was in first place and had 
30,000 points with the first place bonus.

00:17:59.190 --> 00:18:01.530
Amount Won

00:18:00.020 --> 00:18:03.380
And you were in last 
place with minus 20,000.

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:07.860
Amount Won                  Amount Lost

00:18:03.380 --> 00:18:05.600
Taking the ranking bonus into account,

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:06.640
Rank bonus         Rank bonus

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:07.830
the difference between us 
would be 110,000 points.

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:07.860
<b>Points                                                  Points</b>

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:07.850
Point Spread                            Points

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:11.390
Which means that you would 
lose 1,100 CCs of blood

00:18:11.390 --> 00:18:14.370
in just one East-South match.

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:19.530
Were that to happen twice, 
your 200,000 points,

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:22.380
your 2,000 CCs of blood, 
would vanish in a flash.

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:26.820
Still, if you think about 
the other side of that risk,

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:31.050
it means that you have a high chance 
of gaining a large amount of money.

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:35.290
If you think positively, 
it's a great arrangement.

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:39.770
Six East-South matches, 
200,000 points.

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:41.840
A pure one-on-one battle.

00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:44.500
That's the root of Washizu Mahjong.

00:18:45.210 --> 00:18:47.700
The payments will be settled 
after each East-South match.

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:49.480
If you have more points,

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:51.830
you can choose to take money 
or regain some of your blood.

00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:54.640
Or, of course, you can do both.

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:57.440
The winner gets to decide 
how to split the winnings.

00:18:58.090 --> 00:18:59.710
And one more thing.

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:05.220
In Washizu Mahjong, 
there's something like a bonus.

00:19:05.880 --> 00:19:08.220
If there is a direct 
hit on your opponent,

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:11.560
or if you get a tsumo win, 
along with the points,

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:16.230
the equivalent amount of money or 
blood will be transferred, as well.

00:19:16.870 --> 00:19:20.130
The winner decides what 
form of payment it will be.

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:22.370
I'm repeating myself,

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:25.650
but this is a condition that 
only applies to you and me.

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:31.280
With this addition, it becomes more clear 
that it's really a one-on-one contest.

00:19:32.660 --> 00:19:36.220
It's actually quite interesting 
that money or blood

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:38.680
is transferred during the East-South match.

00:19:39.260 --> 00:19:41.180
For example, if you 
keep chasing my money

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:45.720
and choose to not regain some of 
the 1,100 CCs you lost earlier...

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:50.310
...and you happen to deal 
into a yakuman hand...

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:56.170
...you will lose over 320 CCs 
in the middle of the game.

00:19:56.170 --> 00:20:01.510
That means the game could be settled even 
before the second East-South match is over.

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:04.050
You could die.

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:06.670
What do you think?

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:10.210
I bet you won't be able to play carelessly.

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:13.020
You'll start shaking.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:16.510
That's not just a figure of speech, 
you will literally start shaking.

00:20:16.510 --> 00:20:21.150
With each tile, the deepest 
core of your being

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:25.430
will freeze and you'll really start shaking.

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:28.930
That's what I want to see.

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:32.440
That fear, that horror.

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:34.240
I need to see it.

00:20:34.860 --> 00:20:37.670
I need to see it so badly!

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:43.130
So badly that I've killed 
so many men already!

00:20:56.810 --> 00:21:00.500
The genius, Akagi, versus the 
monster, Washizu Iwao.

00:21:00.970 --> 00:21:07.200
The unprecedentedly gruesome game 
of Mahjong is about to begin.

00:22:16.170 --> 00:22:19.130
Next time,  
"The Mahjong Game of Destruction."

00:22:17.150 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>Next episode</b>

00:22:17.150 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>The Mahjong Game of Destruction</b>
